WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.335
-Our next guest
is a very funny comedian.

00:00:02.335 --> 00:00:04.738
His comedy special
"Slow &amp; Steady"

00:00:04.738 --> 00:00:06.139
is streaming now on YouTube.

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:07.574
Let's take a look.

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:09.742
-Was a difficult few months

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:13.379
after the Dahmer show
came out on Netflix.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:15.648
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.055 --> 00:00:25.558
I was getting texts and e-mails

00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:30.062
from people I haven't heard from
in over a decade saying that,

00:00:30.062 --> 00:00:34.000
"The guy on Dahmer's show
looks and sounds like you."

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.403
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:40.339
Couple kids on the street
even said,

00:00:40.339 --> 00:00:42.075
"Hey, Dahmer."

00:00:42.075 --> 00:00:43.809
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.944
I'll be honest,

00:00:45.944 --> 00:00:52.852
if I did even half of the stuff
that Jeffrey Dahmer did,

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.455
my dad would be so pissed off.

00:00:55.455 --> 00:00:56.956
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.992
-Please welcome back to the show
the one, the only Joe Pera.

00:00:59.992 --> 00:01:02.128
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:16.942 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:16.942 --> 00:01:20.245
Welcome back, Joe.
-Thank you very much.

00:01:20.245 --> 00:01:23.316
Hey, Fred, can I come
to your Thousands hair salon?

00:01:23.316 --> 00:01:24.684
-Yes.
-'Cause I could use

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.519
about a thousand more hairs.

00:01:26.519 --> 00:01:30.055
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:33.459
They combed it over real good
backstage, but, yeah.

00:01:33.459 --> 00:01:35.327
-So, Joe, it's so great --

00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:39.666
Again, your ability to do,
you know, banter.

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:42.502
You're back in New York City.

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:44.137
You've been on tour
for over a year.

00:01:44.137 --> 00:01:46.606
How is it to be back
in New York?

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.941
-It's really nice
to be back in New York,

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:51.611
spend some quality time
with my side pieces.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:53.613
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.314
-It's been tough.

00:01:55.314 --> 00:01:56.816
I've been mailing them

00:01:56.816 --> 00:01:59.351
$20 Best Buy gift cards
from the road.

00:01:59.351 --> 00:02:03.089
But that can only last
for so long.

00:02:03.089 --> 00:02:07.093
I don't want to brag,
but I've been buying printer ink

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:10.697
and Nintendo Switch games for
women in three different states.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.732
-Wow.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.967
-Just -- Just -- Just a joke.

00:02:14.967 --> 00:02:16.569
-Oh, that's just a joke.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.538
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.540 --> 00:02:24.176
Did you learn things about the
world while you were touring?

00:02:24.176 --> 00:02:26.145
I mean, you went
so many interesting places.

00:02:26.145 --> 00:02:28.714
-Yeah, it was
really enlightening.

00:02:28.714 --> 00:02:32.018
I mean, did you know
that in Ireland,

00:02:32.018 --> 00:02:35.755
they don't have
Bluetooth technology?

00:02:35.755 --> 00:02:38.190
That's true, and in Australia,

00:02:38.190 --> 00:02:40.826
did you know that
when a baby is born,

00:02:40.826 --> 00:02:43.296
they give him little kick
in the head?

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.064
[ Laughter ]

00:02:47.133 --> 00:02:49.068
That's why they're like that.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:51.070
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:56.743
-I know when you're
out on the road,

00:02:56.743 --> 00:02:57.910
you do a lot of crowd work.

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.812
Do you find out stuff
about people

00:02:59.812 --> 00:03:01.580
from interacting with audiences?

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:03.716
-Yeah, it's probably
my favorite part,

00:03:03.716 --> 00:03:07.953
to do research and then --
yeah, and then find out more

00:03:07.953 --> 00:03:12.191
by talking with the people
in the crowd.

00:03:12.191 --> 00:03:14.060
Yeah, sometimes it's good.

00:03:14.060 --> 00:03:18.864
In Grand Rapids, probably
the drunkest city on tour.

00:03:18.864 --> 00:03:21.701
They were -- Some woman
was yelling at me

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:24.470
to check out
a Frank Lloyd Wright house

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:27.206
over and over again
and wouldn't stop.

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:28.941
So I was yelling back.

00:03:28.941 --> 00:03:32.178
I was saying, "You guys
used to make furniture.

00:03:32.178 --> 00:03:35.415
Now you make craft beer
as your big product.

00:03:35.415 --> 00:03:38.651
What happened?
What happened to you guys?"

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:39.718
-So you were ready with that

00:03:39.718 --> 00:03:41.621
'cause you'd done
research about --

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:44.156
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:46.626
-Yeah, they used to
make more furniture

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:50.797
than almost any other place in
the country at a certain time.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:54.767
-Yeah.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.802
I don't want to make them
feel bad or anything,

00:03:56.802 --> 00:03:58.137
but she wouldn't stop yelling

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.872
about the Frank Lloyd Wright
house.

00:03:59.872 --> 00:04:01.007
-Yeah, so at some point,

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:03.209
you got to give him
the hard truths

00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:06.378
about the falloff
in their furniture production.

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:10.115
-I think we need
great furniture like this stuff.

00:04:10.115 --> 00:04:11.550
-Oh.

00:04:11.550 --> 00:04:13.519
You're so -- so sweet.

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:17.022
You -- Is it true that you
actually did crowd work

00:04:17.022 --> 00:04:19.725
with someone who had --
who had passed out?

00:04:19.725 --> 00:04:22.160
-Yeah, that happened in Aurora.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.196
I do some sleep material,

00:04:24.196 --> 00:04:25.999
so it wasn't like a --

00:04:25.999 --> 00:04:28.601
It's not out of the ordinary

00:04:28.601 --> 00:04:31.704
for them to fall asleep
for periods of time.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:35.308
But the guy was asleep
the entire show.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:37.343
-What do you think happens
when you go to a comedy show

00:04:37.343 --> 00:04:41.213
and fall asleep
right from the beginning?

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:44.850
-I guess --
I mean, his case, he was...

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.087
just drunk and didn't think
about the altitude in Colorado.

00:04:48.087 --> 00:04:49.688
I did -- I personally --

00:04:49.688 --> 00:04:52.524
I fell asleep at
Conner O'Malley's show one time

00:04:52.524 --> 00:04:54.126
'cause I had just moved
that day,

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:56.162
but I wanted to go out
and support my friend.

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.496
-Yeah.
-He actually --

00:04:57.496 --> 00:04:59.565
He broke character to say like,

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:03.136
"Hey, man, you can go home
if you want to."

00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:04.804
-Your special is on YouTube,

00:05:04.804 --> 00:05:07.273
which is really exciting
'cause anyone can see it.

00:05:07.273 --> 00:05:09.909
But also, YouTube
obviously provides people

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:12.111
a chance to leave comments.

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:15.748
Are you the kind of person who
would read the comment section?

00:05:15.748 --> 00:05:18.317
-It gets a little hairy,
and I try not to.

00:05:18.317 --> 00:05:19.785
-Yeah.

00:05:19.785 --> 00:05:24.257
-There was one comment
I did look at in Instagram.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:26.459
I put up the Dahmer joke
that you showed,

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:31.397
and somebody said, "Thank you,
sir, for not doing murder."

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:34.199
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.199 --> 00:05:36.302
You know, ha-ha-ha-ha.

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:40.039
But then a person
underneath said,

00:05:40.039 --> 00:05:44.710
"The dad in the joke is actually
upset because he's gay."

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:47.380
And it's like, I didn't think --

00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:49.448
You know, I don't like
explaining jokes.

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:52.185
That's not fun, and also,
you think that there's, like,

00:05:52.185 --> 00:05:56.054
a bottom level of intelligence
on the Internet,

00:05:56.054 --> 00:05:59.859
and, you know, and, yeah.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:03.729
So I just -- Yeah, it sucks
that you have to explain

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:05.130
that that joke is about --

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:07.600
-I mean, I'd love to give --
Yeah, it's about the murder.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.936
And just 'cause you're here,
where do you stand on murder?

00:06:09.936 --> 00:06:11.671
Just to clear it up, right.

00:06:11.671 --> 00:06:13.539
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.674 --> 00:06:17.743
-It's not okay.
-Alright.

00:06:17.743 --> 00:06:20.212
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:06:20.212 --> 00:06:22.882
A lot of times people
can get a little mealymouthed.

00:06:22.882 --> 00:06:24.483
It's nice that you came out
and just said it.

00:06:24.483 --> 00:06:27.920
-Thank you, yeah, and, no,
being gay is good, great even.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:31.623
So, yeah, the joke is about
murdering and eating people.

00:06:31.623 --> 00:06:35.260
-Yeah, well, I think we can all
laugh at it a little bit more

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.495
now that we know that.

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:37.629
-I hope so.

00:06:37.629 --> 00:06:39.164
I just --
It never occurred to me

00:06:39.164 --> 00:06:40.733
that it could be taken that way.
-Yeah.

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:42.268
Well, now we've cleared it up.

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:44.136
And it's a wonderful special.

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:45.537
And it's always so great
to have you back here.

00:06:45.537 --> 00:06:47.106
You guys, that's Joe Pera.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:48.941
"Slow &amp; Steady"
streaming on YouTube.

00:06:48.941 --> 00:06:52.745
We'll be right back
with Chef Ayesha Nurdjaja.

